            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen caused by placenta percreta in the second trimester.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>146-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A woman with a history of &quot;in utero&quot; diethylstilbestrol exposure but no prior uterine surgery presented with an acute abdomen at 21 weeks' gestation. She had hemoperitoneum associated with placenta percreta.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
